{"item_id": "core-b3-numeric-7ed8187df3", "model": "gemini/gemini-3.5-flash", "status": "ok", "parsed": {"answer": 2503.5, "unit": "W", "stage_answers": {"S1": {"value": "Convection and radiation; total heat loss is the sum of both modes: Q_total = Q_conv + Q_rad.", "unit": ""}, "S2": {"value": "A = pi * D * L = 0.5 * pi ≈ 1.5708 m^2. Q_conv = h * A * (T_s - T_inf) and Q_rad = eps * sigma * A * (T_s^4 - T_surr^4).", "unit": ""}, "S3": {"value": "Q_conv = 1256.6 W, Q_rad = 1246.9 W.", "unit": ""}, "S4": {"value": "Q_total = 2503.5 W.", "unit": ""}}, "option_verdicts": [], "ambiguous": false, "ambiguity_reason": "", "working": "A = pi * D * L = pi * 0.10 * 5.0 = 0.5 * pi ≈ 1.5708 m^2.\nQ_conv = h * A * (T_s - T_inf) = 8.0 * (0.5 * pi) * (400 - 300) = 400 * pi ≈ 1256.64 W.\nQ_rad = eps * sigma * A * (T_s^4 - T_surr^4) = 0.80 * 5.67e-8 * (0.5 * pi) * (400^4 - 300^4) = 396.9 * pi ≈ 1246.90 W.\nQ_total = Q_conv + Q_rad = 796.9 * pi ≈ 2503.54 W."}, "label_map": {}}
{"item_id": "core-b3-numeric-7ed8187df3", "model": "gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview", "status": "ok", "parsed": {"answer": 2503.5, "unit": "W", "stage_answers": {"S1": {"value": "The two modes are natural convection and net radiation. They are combined by adding the individual heat loss rates: Q_total = Q_conv + Q_rad.", "unit": ""}, "S2": {"value": "Surface area A = pi * D * L = pi * 0.10 * 5.0 = 0.5*pi m^2. Rate equations: Q_conv = h * A * (T_s - T_inf) and Q_rad = epsilon * sigma * A * (T_s^4 - T_surr^4).", "unit": ""}, "S3": {"value": "Q_conv = 8.0 * (0.5*pi) * (400 - 300) = 400*pi = 1256.6 W. Q_rad = 0.80 * 5.67e-8 * (0.5*pi) * (400^4 - 300^4) = 396.9*pi = 1246.9 W.", "unit": ""}, "S4": {"value": "Q_total = 1256.6 + 1246.9 = 2503.5 W.", "unit": ""}}, "option_verdicts": [], "ambiguous": false, "ambiguity_reason": "", "working": "Area A = pi * 0.1 * 5 = 1.5708 m^2. Convection loss Q_conv = h * A * (T_s - T_inf) = 8 * 1.5708 * 100 = 1256.6 W. Radiation loss Q_rad = epsilon * sigma * A * (T_s^4 - T_surr^4) = 0.8 * 5.67e-8 * 1.5708 * (400^4 - 300^4) = 1246.9 W. Total loss Q_total = 1256.6 + 1246.9 = 2503.5 W."}, "label_map": {}}
{"item_id": "core-b3-numeric-7ed8187df3", "model": "gemini/gemini-3.6-flash", "status": "ok", "parsed": {"answer": 2503.53, "unit": "W", "stage_answers": {"S1": {"value": "Natural convection and thermal radiation act in parallel at the surface; total heat loss is the sum of both modes: q_total = q_conv + q_rad.", "unit": ""}, "S2": {"value": "Area A = pi * D * L = 0.5*pi ≈ 1.5708 m^2. q_conv = h * A * (T_s - T_inf); q_rad = eps * sigma * A * (T_s^4 - T_surr^4).", "unit": ""}, "S3": {"value": "q_conv = 1256.64 W, q_rad = 1246.90 W.", "unit": ""}, "S4": {"value": "Total heat loss = 2503.53 W.", "unit": ""}}, "option_verdicts": [], "ambiguous": false, "ambiguity_reason": "", "working": "Surface Area A = pi * 0.10 m * 5.0 m = 0.5*pi m^2 ≈ 1.5708 m^2.\nConvection heat loss q_conv = h * A * (T_s - T_inf) = 8.0 * (0.5*pi) * (400 - 300) = 400*pi W ≈ 1256.64 W.\nRadiation heat loss q_rad = eps * sigma * A * (T_s^4 - T_surr^4) = 0.80 * 5.67e-8 * (0.5*pi) * (400^4 - 300^4) = 396.9*pi W ≈ 1246.90 W.\nTotal heat loss q_total = q_conv + q_rad = 796.9*pi W ≈ 2503.53 W."}, "label_map": {}}
{"item_id": "core-b3-numeric-d5cf432a2e", "model": "gemini/gemini-3.5-flash", "status": "ok", "parsed": {"answer": 137050, "unit": "W/m^2", "stage_answers": {"S1": {"value": "Nucleate pool boiling, Rohsenow correlation", "unit": ""}, "S2": {"value": "399.3", "unit": ""}, "S3": {"value": "0.8169", "unit": ""}, "S4": {"value": "137050", "unit": ""}}, "option_verdicts": [], "ambiguous": false, "ambiguity_reason": "", "working": "1. Buoyancy factor: [9.81 * (957.9 - 0.5955) / 58.9e-3]^0.5 = 399.30 1/m.\n2. Dimensionless ratio: (4217 * 10) / (0.0130 * 2.257e6 * 1.76^1.0) = 0.81686.\n3. Heat flux q'' = (279e-6 * 2.257e6) * 399.30 * (0.81686)^3 = 629.703 * 399.30 * 0.54505 = 137050 W/m^2."}, "label_map": {}}
